@startuml
title TMFC039 : Agreement Management -- eTOM/SID ABE Links
' The source image's own footer literally reads "TMFC020 - Agreement Management"
' (an apparent mislabel/typo for TMFC039 in the source PDF) -- reproduced as-is,
' not corrected, since this redraw is of exactly what the image shows.

class "L2 - Party Agreement Management" as L2PartyAgreementManagement <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class Agreement <<SID Data Entity>>
class AgreementItem <<SID Data Entity>>
class AgreementTermOrCondition <<SID Data Entity>>

' eTOM activity <-> SID ABE link. Per the image's own legend, an arrow from the
' eTOM activity towards the SID ABE means information produced by the activity;
' the reverse arrow means information consumed by the activity. The image draws
' this pair as a single double-headed arrow, i.e. both hold simultaneously.
L2PartyAgreementManagement --> Agreement : produces
Agreement --> L2PartyAgreementManagement : is consumed by

' SID entity <-> SID entity links. NOTE: the image's legend only defines arrow
' meaning for eTOM-activity <-> SID-ABE arrows -- it does not define what an
' arrow directly between two SID entities means. These six arrows are
' reproduced with exactly the direction drawn in the image (each pair of
' entities is linked by two separate, adjacent single-headed arrows, one each
' way), with no "produces"/"is consumed by" semantic invented for them.
Agreement --> AgreementItem
AgreementItem --> Agreement
Agreement --> AgreementTermOrCondition
AgreementTermOrCondition --> Agreement
AgreementItem --> AgreementTermOrCondition
AgreementTermOrCondition --> AgreementItem

footer TMFC020 - Agreement Management (as printed in the source image)
@enduml
